N5008 [temp.pre]/1, [temp.spec]/4, [temp.mem]/1: a static data member
template of a class (template).  Each specialization is a distinct
variable (was: the second specialization was a "redeclaration" of the
first, surfacing as "found no match"); its initializer may name the
enclosing class template's parameters (`same<T, X>`) and be referenced
from a member function template body or a constructor mem-initializer
with the member template's own parameter; a repeated reference finds the
existing specialization.  Also: the template arguments of a variable
template-id are type-checked at the point of use
(`std::in_place_index<idx<Tp>>` naming a class member, [basic.lookup.unqual]).
